0,Kadiwéu - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kadiwéu,"November 4, 2025 - The Kadiweu today live in the Kadiweu Indigenous Land, a large reserve established in 1903, in the Brazilian state of Mato Grosso do Sul in the municipality of Porto Murtinho, between the Serra de Bodoquena and the Nabileque and Aquidavão rivers.",Kadiwéu,Guaykuruan
1,Kadiwéu language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kadiweu_language,"March 8, 2026 - The name Kadiweu has variants such as Kaduveo, Caduveo, Kadivéu, and Kadiveo. This language is spoken near the Brazil-Paraguay border in the state of Mato Grosso do Sul. The nearest town is Bodoquena, which is 60 kilometers away.",Kadiwéu,Guaykuruan
2,Kadiwéu - Indigenous Peoples in Brazil,https://pib.socioambiental.org/en/Povo:Kadiwéu,"Kadiwéu art is also expressed in the songs of the older women, in the music of the flute and drum players, and in the collective dances.",Kadiwéu,Guaykuruan
3,"Kadiwéu Language (KBC) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kbc/,Kadiwéu is a stable indigenous language of Brazil. It belongs to the Guaykuruan language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Kadiwéu,Guaykuruan
